    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FALSIFIABILITY",
      "narration_text": "R A G fixes a lot. Answers are grounded in your text, they can cite it, and you update documents instead of retraining. But it's only as good as retrieval. If the right passage isn't found, or word overlap misleads the scorer, the answer is built on the wrong page. Real systems, Medhavy included, use proper search indexes for exactly this reason.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "lane": "remotion",
        "motion": "reveal",
